{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-034",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 34,
  "title": "Job 34",
  "display_title": "Job 34",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 34,
  "sortOrder": 18034,
  "verseCount": 37,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Furthermore Elihu answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Hear my words, O ye wise men; and give ear unto me, ye that have knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For the ear trieth words, as the mouth tasteth meat.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Let us choose to us judgment: let us know among ourselves what is good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For Job hath said, I am righteous: and God hath taken away my judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Should I lie against my right? my wound is incurable without transgression.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "What man is like Job, who drinketh up scorning like water?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Which goeth in company with the workers of iniquity, and walketh with wicked men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For he hath said, It profiteth a man nothing that he should delight himself with God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Therefore hearken unto me ye men of understanding: far be it from God, that he should do wickedness; and from the Almighty, that he should commit iniquity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For the work of a man shall he render unto him, and cause every man to find according to his ways.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Yea, surely God will not do wickedly, neither will the Almighty pervert judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Who hath given him a charge over the earth? or who hath disposed the whole world?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "If he set his heart upon man, if he gather unto himself his spirit and his breath;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "All flesh shall perish together, and man shall turn again unto dust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "If now thou hast understanding, hear this: hearken to the voice of my words.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Shall even he that hateth right govern? and wilt thou condemn him that is most just?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Is it fit to say to a king, Thou art wicked? and to princes, Ye are ungodly?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "How much less to him that accepteth not the persons of princes, nor regardeth the rich more than the poor? for they all are the work of his hands.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "In a moment shall they die, and the people shall be troubled at midnight, and pass away: and the mighty shall be taken away without hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "For his eyes are upon the ways of man, and he seeth all his goings.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "There is no darkness, nor shadow of death, where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For he will not lay upon man more than right; that he should enter into judgment with God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "He shall break in pieces mighty men without number, and set others in their stead.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Therefore he knoweth their works, and he overturneth them in the night, so that they are destroyed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He striketh them as wicked men in the open sight of others;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Because they turned back from him, and would not consider any of his ways:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "So that they cause the cry of the poor to come unto him, and he heareth the cry of the afflicted.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "When he giveth quietness, who then can make trouble? and when he hideth his face, who then can behold him? whether it be done against a nation, or against a man only:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "That the hypocrite reign not, lest the people be ensnared.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Surely it is meet to be said unto God, I have borne chastisement, I will not offend any more:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "That which I see not teach thou me: if I have done iniquity, I will do no more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Should it be according to thy mind? he will recompense it, whether thou refuse, or whether thou choose; and not I: therefore speak what thou knowest.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Let men of understanding tell me, and let a wise man hearken unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Job hath spoken without knowledge, and his words were without wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "My desire is that Job may be tried unto the end because of his answers for wicked men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:34:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "For he addeth rebellion unto his sin, he clappeth his hands among us, and multiplieth his words against God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 34:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:34:37"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
